flowchart TB
  accTitle: Four evidence relation categories E1 to E4
  accDescr: Four independent categories describe the relationship between a historical mechanism and a modern correspondence: documented lineage, structural migration, functional approximation, and structural convergence without evidence of transfer.
  subgraph E1["E1 · Documented lineage"]
    E1A["Modern source explicitly names the historical architecture and connects it to this mechanism"]
  end
  subgraph E2["E2 · Structural migration"]
    E2A["Implemented source-like state plus corresponding control, transition, or learning edge"]
  end
  subgraph E3["E3 · Functional approximation"]
    E3A["Comparable control problem and observable function; materially different organization"]
  end
  subgraph E4["E4 · Structural convergence"]
    E4A["Comparable node–edge structure; no transfer evidence found, stated explicitly"]
  end
  classDef c1 fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef c2 fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef c3 fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef c4 fill:#F0F0FF,stroke:#5B4FBE,color:#1C1C1E
  class E1A c1
  class E2A c2
  class E3A c3
  class E4A c4
